id: P-cross-study
name: Cross Study
description: Research an array of GitHub projects, tools, or sites and produce a competitive/opportunity analysis report evaluating overlaps with Paradigm, new tool ideas, product value, and concerns.
trigger:
  - cross study
  - competitive analysis
  - research projects
  - evaluate tools
  - compare with paradigm
tags:
  - research
  - strategy
  - competitive-analysis
  - private
symbols: []
steps:
  - action: verify
    notes: User provides an array of GitHub repos, websites, or tools to research
  - action: run
    notes: 'For each project: fetch README, docs, and key source files. Understand what it does, its architecture, and target audience.'
  - action: create
    target: docs/private/cross-studies/{study-name}.md
    notes: 'Create report with 4 sections: (1) Overlaps with Paradigm — features/concepts that already exist in Paradigm, (2) New Tools Paradigm Could Create — gaps or ideas inspired by the project, (3) Overall Product Value — what makes it compelling, market fit, adoption signals, (4) Further Thoughts / Concerns — security, maintainability, scope creep, licensing, etc. Include a summary matrix at the top mapping each project to these 4 dimensions.'
  - action: verify
    notes: Report lives in docs/private/cross-studies/ which is gitignored — never committed to public repo
recorded_at: '2026-03-10T17:06:25.324Z'
last_verified: '2026-03-10T17:06:25.324Z'
verified_by: claude-opus-4-6
status: current
